mapping "D229A.1" source="D229A" target="400096001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source D229A SNOMED CT 400096001 = Intraepidermal pigmented nevus, unspecified site (a
        junctional-level melanocytic nevus confined to the intraepidermal compartment). No SNOMED CT
        concept with the exact phrase exists in the mirror; the closest standard concept is (Melanocytic
        nevus), the Athena canonical target mapped from ICD-10 D22 (45595739 Maps to 4271013 OMOP id,
        concept_code 400096001). Target is broader; the source is a specific intraepidermal histologic
        pattern. Moderate confidence because the target loses the histologic specificity
        (intraepidermal) and the pigmented qualifier.
        """
}
mapping "D229B.1" source="D229B" target="30494009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source D229B SNOMED CT 30494009 = Junctional pigmented nevus (junction-type), unspecified site.
        Target (Junctional nevus). Same clinical-histologic concept; the source additionally specifies
        but all junctional nevi are by definition melanocytic/pigmented, so this is essentially an
        equivalence. High rather than exact because the source string includes the qualifier and an
        unspecified-site framing while the SNOMED CT bare concept is site-unspecified; the Athena ICD-10
        D22 base crosswalk points to a different broader concept (400096001).
        """
}
mapping "D229C.1" source="D229C" target="112681002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source D229C SNOMED CT 112681002 = Intradermal pigmented nevus, unspecified site. Target
        (Intradermal nevus). Same clinical-histologic concept; the source adds the qualifier but
        intradermal nevus is by definition a melanocytic nevus, so essentially equivalent. High rather
        than exact because of the pigmented qualifier and because no ICD-10→SNOMED CT crosswalk exists for
        D22.9 subcodes in the mirror.
        """
}
mapping "D229D.1" source="D229D" target="254805008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source D229D SNOMED CT 254805008 = Compound pigmented nevus, unspecified site (compound = both
        junctional and dermal components). Target (Compound nevus of skin). Same clinical-histologic
        entity; the source adds but compound nevus is by definition melanocytic/pigmented. High rather
        than exact because the target is skin-site-qualified and no ICD-10→SNOMED CT crosswalk exists for
        D22.9 subcodes.
        """
}
mapping "D229E.1" source="D229E" target="400096001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=40 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source D229E SNOMED CT 400096001 =, unspecified site. The phrase is not an established
        clinical/histologic entity in WHO/IARC-recognized classifications or in the SNOMED CT mirror (no
        SNOMED CT concept exists for this term). The most plausible reading is an obsolete Swedish
        histochemical descriptor for a melanocytic nevus variant. Best defensible target is (Melanocytic
        nevus) - the Athena canonical target for ICD-10 D22 (45595739 Maps to 4271013 OMOP id). Target
        is much broader. Low confidence: the source meaning is genuinely ambiguous and no closer
        standard concept exists; recorded to preserve the lead rather than assert equivalence.
        """
}
